{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.OrientedSkein.Model.GLnOSFaithful","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.Model.GLnOSFaithful","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.OrientedSkein.Model.GLnFaithful","lean:module:QOU.OrientedSkein.Model.GLnClosureLift"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.OS_heckeAction_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.OS_heckeAction_injective","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnOSFaithful.lean#L141-L153","doc":"**Faithfulness inside `OS`.**  For `m + 1 ≤ n`, Brundan's\n`ι_{m+1} : H_{m+1}(q) → End_{OS(q, qi, q^n, [n]_q)}(E^{⊗(m+1)})` is injective, over any\ncommutative ring with `q * qi = 1`: the Hecke algebra embeds in the endomorphisms of every tensor\npower `E^{⊗r}`, `r ≤ n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.lift_heckeAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.lift_heckeAction","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnOSFaithful.lean#L131-L139","doc":"**The lift of Brundan's `ι_r` is the `GL_n` Hecke action, conjugated by `Φ`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.conjAlg_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.conjAlg_injective","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnOSFaithful.lean#L124-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.conjAlg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.conjAlg","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnOSFaithful.lean#L112-L122","doc":"Conjugation by an isomorphism, as an algebra map on endomorphism algebras. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.mapEndAlg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.mapEndAlg","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnOSFaithful.lean#L98-L109","doc":"An `R`-linear functor induces an algebra map on endomorphism algebras. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.map_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.map_gen","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnOSFaithful.lean#L85-L95","doc":"**The lift carries the OS crossing on strands `i, i+1` to the `GL_n` crossing**, up to `Φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.map_gen_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.map_gen_zero","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnOSFaithful.lean#L65-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.map_gen_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.map_gen_succ","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnOSFaithful.lean#L54-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.Φ_succ_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.Φ_succ_inv","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnOSFaithful.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.Φ_succ_hom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.Φ_succ_hom","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnOSFaithful.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.Φ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.GLn.Φ","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/Model/GLnOSFaithful.lean#L46-L49","doc":"`G (E^{⊗k}) ≅ X^{⊗k}`, componentwise identity up to the definitional unfolding of words. ","signatureChunk":0}]}